# Confirm before the first release: affiliation, ORCID, and the co-author list.
# Once the repo is pushed and the Zenodo integration is switched on, Zenodo mints
# a DOI on each GitHub release — add it under `doi:` and to the README badge.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FluLens in published work, please cite it as below."
title: FluLens
abstract: >-
  A viewer and reviewer for influenza variant calls produced by the Flumina
  pipeline. Displays a run as samples by codons, one cell per call, coloured by
  allele frequency, with per-variant read-level evidence, strand-bias
  assessment, FluMut marker screening and selection results.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hutter
    given-names: Carl R.
    email: carl.hutter@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/flu-crew/FluLens"
url: "https://flu-crew.github.io/FluLens/"
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-03
keywords:
  - influenza
  - variant calling
  - low-frequency variants
  - genomic surveillance
  - visualisation
